verdicts.fold_scope_text:
Re-scope (S238, per ADR 0003a decision 8 and data-standards open item #4; Nghiệp to confirm): the original premise of granting shared.job to a second repo is superseded by docs/adr/0003a-per-owner-job-tables.md (one job table per owner schema). This issue now delivers roadmap X6 (docs/architecture/data-standards/02-data-management.md §12):
(1) a reference job DDL template in apps/AA-CIS-App/shared/jobs/ (CIS 174 columns, status set, owner kind-prefix CHECK, lease CHECK, indexes including the finished_at retention index, and queue autovacuum settings), with a per-owner CI test comparing each <schema>.job to it;
(2) a bk-NNN migration adding cancel_requested, progress, cost_usd, parent_job_id and the finished_at index to booking.job, plus release-or-requeue of running jobs on shutdown in the Booking runner (C6.2c);
(3) a Booking deploy job guard in apps/AA-Booking/.github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml that blocks while booking.job has queued/running rows (C6.3a), replacing the stale "No job guard" comment at line 16;
(4) an idle-check step in infra/AA-CIS-Infra/.github/workflows/db-migrate.yml that, before apply, loops over every owner's job table (shared.job, booking.job, and any later <schema>.job, ideally read from owners.yaml once X1 lands) and fails if any has queued/running jobs, so it replaces the manual jobcheck2.py (C6.3b, DM-11.4);
(5) a per-owner job backlog-age alarm in Terraform (accounts/aa365/observability_ecosys.tf → aws_sns_topic.alerts) firing when the oldest queued job is more than 15 min old or a running job exceeds 2× the kind's expected_seconds, with missing data treated as not breaching (C4.1, C4.1a);
(6) moving the acp_runs readers to shared.job.
tripplanner.job (needed before the TripPlanner outbox PII redaction, DM-7.2) is created from the same template when its first kind is cut.

Done when:
- the template file and the per-owner comparison test are green in CI for CIS and Booking;
- the bk-NNN migration is applied via DB Migrate and the booking.job columns are visible in db-schema-reference.md;
- a Booking deploy is blocked by a seeded queued bk_ job and passes when the table is idle;
- a DB Migrate apply is refused while any owner's job table is busy and logs which table;
- the backlog-age alarm(s) exist in CloudWatch from terraform apply;
- grep shows no runtime acp_runs reader;
- the ADR 0003 status table and schema-ownership.md point to ADR 0003a.
